Z||000000||fropuff||05-13-2001||02:59 PM||||Hey guys.  I've talked about this with Darklord before, but I was wondering if a Vortec 350 would fit in an AWD Chev Astro cargo van.  I'm going to be looking for a winter vehicle soon, and it would be ideal if I could use the engine from our totalled 96 Silverado, if the insurance company will let us keep it.  I know that some people have put 350s in Astros, but I was wondering if this is any different.  Here's the thing though...the 350 is for a 2WD, and I want to put it into an AWD Astro.  Will this work?  Thanks a lot!   <BR><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||4
Z||000001||fropuff||05-14-2001||04:26 PM||||Anyone?   Thanks!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||2xsess||05-16-2001||07:53 PM||||I'm not sure about the differences in the engine as far as fitting in the engine bay but if you use the AWD trnsmission/transaxle there should be no reason why the engine won't bolt up to it.<P>...I think  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||05-16-2001||11:05 PM||||Thanks for the reply.  I was asking if it would work with the tranny because my brother asked the mechanic if a Vortec would fit in a 5-speed S-10, and he said it won't because of the bellhousing or something.  I just think a Vortec Astro would kick ass.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks again! ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||05-17-2001||07:37 PM||||A V8 will bolt up to a 4.3 tranny but not the 2.8 I know a TPI 350 will fit in the engine bay but they had to relocate the battery or something. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||05-17-2001||11:35 PM||||Well, that's good, because I'd get a 4.3L anyway.  I'm going to search the net and see if I can find one with a Vortec in it.  Don't you think it'd kick ass?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||05-18-2001||01:26 AM||||Yeah, it would put you along the lines of thh Syclone/Typhoon people. I Don't think they put the smaller V6's in AWD Astros (I really don't know if they put them in any of them actually.) If it's a 93 or later Astro it will have the vortec 4.3 in it. Not that it really matters.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||05-23-2001||05:05 PM||||Well, I was surfin around and came across this:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.y-t-g.com/astronews.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.y-t-g.com/astronews.html</A> <P>It's pretty sweet-ass!  It gets the 1/4 mile in mid-14s and 0-60 in 5.9 seconds.  You've gotta look at the burnout pics!  This is a 2WD, but I think I may get one as well.  The MN winters get pretty bad, but I'd get some good snow tires.  The Cutlass did okay w/o snow tires.  My brother's thinking of getting an 89 Silverado w/ a 350, so he will swap in the Vortec.  However, I'd get to keep the 350.  The performance won't be as good, but still good nonetheless.  What do you think?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||1
